{"source":"state-provider","target":"ext:react-context","type":"ANALOGOUS_TO","note":"Both provide hierarchical state, but Neo.mjs providers use bind:{} on reactive configs — no subtree re-rendering. Providers survive cross-window teleportation."}
{"source":"state-provider","target":"ext:vuex-pinia","type":"ANALOGOUS_TO","note":"Both manage shared state, but Neo.mjs providers are hierarchical (parent-child scoped) rather than global singletons."}
{"source":"reactive-configs","target":"ext:vue-reactivity","type":"ANALOGOUS_TO","note":"Both are push-based, but Neo.mjs uses explicit trailing-underscore opt-in with named lifecycle hooks vs Vue's Proxy-based auto-tracking."}
{"source":"reactive-configs","target":"ext:react-usestate","type":"ANALOGOUS_TO","note":"Both trigger updates on change, but Neo.mjs configs are class-level declarations with named beforeSet/afterSet hooks — not per-render-cycle hooks."}
{"source":"pull-reactivity","target":"ext:vue-computed","type":"ANALOGOUS_TO","note":"Both auto-track dependencies and re-execute on change. Neo.mjs Effects use the same trailing-underscore reactive system as configs."}
{"source":"json-first-vdom","target":"ext:react-jsx","type":"ANALOGOUS_TO","note":"Both describe UI declaratively. JSX compiles to createElement calls; Neo.mjs VDOM is raw JSON — no compilation, serializable across workers."}
{"source":"multi-threading","target":"ext:react-concurrent","type":"ANALOGOUS_TO","note":"React Concurrent Mode simulates priority scheduling on one thread. Neo.mjs uses actual OS-level threads (Web Workers) for true parallelism."}
{"source":"component-composition","target":"ext:react-children","type":"ANALOGOUS_TO","note":"Both use nested component trees. React uses JSX children props; Neo.mjs uses the items config array with declarative JSON."}
{"source":"observable-event-system","target":"ext:eventemitter","type":"ANALOGOUS_TO","note":"Both provide pub/sub. Neo.mjs Observable is a mixin applied via the class system, not a standalone class. DOM events delegate through VDOM to component methods."}
{"source":"zero-build-dev","target":"ext:vite-dev","type":"ANALOGOUS_TO","note":"Both serve native ES modules in development. Vite uses a dev server with HMR; Neo.mjs loads raw source files directly in the browser — no server needed."}
